Now let me understand the exact bug. In `punycode_decode`:

```c
for (b = j = 0;  j < input_length;  ++j)  if (delim(input[j])) b = j;
if (b >= max_out) return punycode_big_output;

for (j = 0;  j < b;  ++j) {
    if (!basic(input[j])) return punycode_bad_input;
    output[out++] = input[j];
}
b += delim(input[b]);
```

The issue: when `input_length == 0`, `b = 0`, and `delim(input[0])` reads `input[0]`. If `input` is a pointer to an empty buffer (e.g., from `u32_to_u8` with count 0), then `input[0]` might be uninitialized memory.

